---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { directoryStats, href, site } from '../lib/data';
import { breadcrumbNode, pageGraph, webPageNode } from '../lib/schema';

const title = 'About this RV and boat storage directory';
const description =
  'How RV Storage Finder checks facility pages, why unknown amenities say not listed, and how a new city file becomes city, state, and filter pages.';
const path = '/about/';
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { label: 'About', path },
];
const schema = pageGraph([
  webPageNode({ title, description, path, dateModified: directoryStats().latest }),
  breadcrumbNode(crumbs),
]);
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path={path} schema={schema}>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <h1>About this directory</h1>
    <p>
      RV Storage Finder is a static directory of RV and boat storage. It is built for people comparing
      covered RV storage near Tampa, boat storage with power near Phoenix, or a published monthly price
      in Houston, Orlando, or Dallas-Fort Worth.
    </p>
    <h2>What gets recorded</h2>
    <p>
      Each facility comes from a public page: the operator’s site, or a marketplace listing when that is
      the page we could open. The card stores the name, address, phone, website, vehicle types, cover
      type, length, clearance, power, dump station, wash station, gate, cameras, 24-hour access, a price
      note, and a waitlist note. The source URL and the date that page was opened sit on the card.
    </p>
    <p>
      Yes means the source says the amenity is available. No means the source says it is not. Not listed
      means the source is silent. A missing price is not a guess, and a national average is not copied
      onto a facility that did not print a rate.
    </p>
    <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
    <p>
      It does not invent facilities to fill a city. It does not claim to list every lot in a metro. It
      does not publish star ratings. It is not the storage facility, and calling a number on a card
      reaches that business, not this directory.
    </p>
    <h2>How a new city appears</h2>
    <p>
      Listings live in one YAML file per city. Adding that file creates the city page, adds the city to
      its state page, and creates filter pages for covered, enclosed, outdoor, power, dump, boat, and
      published-price views wherever at least one listing matches. The steps are in
      <a href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/PUBLISHING.md`}>PUBLISHING.md</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={href('/disclosure/')}>Affiliate disclosure and privacy</a> explains the Neighbor and
      SpareFoot links. <a href={href('/guide/')}>The cost guide</a> explains how to read a monthly rate.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
